  "limitations": [
    "Attribution results are SYNTHETIC PERSONA RETRIEVAL, not validated human authorship attribution. Personas are generated with known parameters, so recovering them recovers the generator.",
    "Sample size is small: 12 clustered services across 4 clusters, 20 personas. Confidence intervals are reported because the point estimates alone would overstate what the sample supports.",
    "The test split holds out 2 of 4 clusters, so evaluation is on unseen operators by construction, but the test set is small and the interval correspondingly wide.",
    "Frequency filtering addresses widespread vendor-default artefacts and not coincidental ones. The coincidental class needs a maintained blocklist of known defaults, which this implementation does not have.",
    "Rules without an implemented negative fixture: ['apache_version_banner', 'backup_file', 'dot_env', 'etag_pattern', 'http_header_order', 'nginx_version_banner', 'timezone_leak']. Their false-positive rates are measured only against true positives and are therefore optimistic; this is reported rather than left implied.",
    "Provenance establishes byte consistency against a recorded digest. It is not chain of custody and does not establish admissibility."
  ]
